 follows:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{number of green crates}: \\textrm{total number of crates}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the number of green crates. There are $5$ green crates.\n- Next, we count the total number of crates. There are $8+5 = 13$ crates.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of green crates to total crates is $5:13$." 13194139534723 17592186045417 false] [17592186073452 1071 "The ratio of red marbles to blue marbles in a  bag is $7:8.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073452 1071 "The ratio of red marbles to blue marbles in a bag is $7:8$. What is the meaning of this ratio?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 false] [17592186073452 1074 "If the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles is ${\\color{red}{7}}:{\\color{blue}{8}}$, it means that there are ${\\color{red}{7}}$ red marbles for every ${\\color{blue}{8}}$ blue marbles." 13194139534723 17592186045417 false] [17592186073452 1074 "If the ratio of red marbles to blue marbles is ${\\color{red}{7}}:{\\color{blue}{8}},$ it means that there are ${\\color{red}{7}}$ red marbles for every ${\\color{blue}{8}}$ blue marbles." 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434178 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434180 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434182 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434185 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073735 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434190 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434181 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434184 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434186 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434188 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073736 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434189 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434177 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434179 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434183 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073737 1038 #edb/ref 17592186434187 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186073954 1050 420.0 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186074402 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186074402 1071 "The ratio of male to the female members of a chess club is $2: 3$. What is the meaning of this ratio?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 false] [17592186074402 1071 "The ratio of male to the female members of a chess club is $2:3.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186074402 1074 "If the ratio of male members to female members is $2:3,$ it means that there are $2$ male members for every $3$ female members." 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186075037 1064 "A **ratio** is a mathematical statement that expresses the relative sizes of two quantities.\n\nAs an example, let's look at the triangles and circles below.\n\n![](images/48/4865786ce55e0ec3fc1747ece4ea962425a3f83b2a45c7980f52719522318c82.png)\n\nWe can express the ratio of the number of circles to the number of triangles as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{\\textrm{number of circles}}}: {\\color{red}{\\textrm{number of triangles}}}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of circles. There are $\\color{blue}5$ circles.\n- Next, we count the number of triangles. There are $\\color{red}2$ triangles.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of circles to triangles is ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}2}$.\n\nWe can describe this ratio in words as follows:\n\n> *The ratio of circles to triangles is ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}2}$ because there are ${\\color{blue}5}$ circles*for every*${\\color{red}{2}}$ triangles.*" 13194139534723 17592186045417 false] [17592186075037 1064 "A **ratio** is a mathematical statement that expresses the relative sizes of two quantities.\n\nAs an example, let's look at the triangles and circles below. \n\n![](images/48/4865786ce55e0ec3fc1747ece4ea962425a3f83b2a45c7980f52719522318c82.png)\n\nWe can express the ratio of the number of circles to the number of triangles as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{\\textrm{number of circles}}} : {\\color{red}{\\textrm{number of triangles}}}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of circles. There are $\\color{blue}5$ circles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of triangles. There are $\\color{red}2$ triangles.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of circles to triangles is ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}2}.$\n\nWe can describe this ratio in words as follows:\n\n*The ratio of circles to triangles is  ${\\color{blue}5}:{\\color{red}2}$ because there are ${\\color{blue}5}$ circles *for every* ${\\color{red}{2}}$ triangles.*" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434099 1080 "3:4" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434099 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434099 1083 #uuid "091970d9-19e9-5c8f-9d4c-37f6882cad35" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434100 1080 "5:7" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434100 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434100 1083 #uuid "091bb0b2-72e2-5c50-857e-ccded7de6ded" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434101 1080 "The birthday party has exactly $7$ children" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434101 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434101 1083 #uuid "0b18d8df-3fc8-5d58-a9fd-1e8f50306474" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434102 1080 "3:2" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434102 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [1759