 are $4$ boys for every $7$ children at the birthday party.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $7$ children at the birthday party, $4$ of them are boys.\"" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434178 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434165 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434178 1069 "q-70129" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434178 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434178 1071 "![](images/4f/4f6801c9bb82b4ba0a3ac2d16bf9d06799d0349ff718fbc31429cd74d054bcbe.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to hexagons?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434178 1072 #uuid "0ff410a3-0c6f-5988-88a5-79160a3d1565" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434178 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the number of hexagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{number of hexagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of hexagons. There are $3$ hexagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to hexagons is $2:3.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434179 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434172 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434179 1069 "q-60097" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434179 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434179 1071 "The ratio of dogs to the total number of pets in a veterinary clinic is $2:5.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434179 1072 #uuid "1f1c065d-26db-5359-ab36-7049627505ee" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434179 1074 "If the ratio of dogs to total pets is $2:5,$ it means that there are $2$ dogs for every $5$ pets in the clinic.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $5$ pets in the clinic, $2$ of them are dogs.\"" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434180 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434171 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434180 1069 "q-70132" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434180 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434180 1071 "![](images/ea/eab3931ef4d46de23144f52420557e790a7e041231fec22d6819891e8e92ab16.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of hexagons to pentagons?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434180 1072 #uuid "30f78782-46a8-5fef-93fa-62c3bc5d1001" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434180 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $2$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $3$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $2:3.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434161 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434168 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1069 "q-235954" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1071 "Matt decides to distribute some candy to his best friends. The following table shows the number of candies each of his friends received. \n\n| Friends | Rose | Peter | Adriana | Vanessa | Helen | Luis | Jason |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Candies | $5$ | $6$ | $10$ | $9$ | $4$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat is the ratio of friends who received at least $8$ pieces of candy to those who received less than $8$ pieces of candy?\n\nThe required ratio is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1072 #uuid "342633b7-0af2-5736-9e7c-f7ff7859c8c8" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434181 1074 "From the table, there are $2$ friends (Adriana and Vanessa) who received at least $8$ candies.\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ friends (Rose, Peter, Helen, Luis, and Jason) who received less than $8$ candies.\n\nSo the ratio of friends who received at least $8$ pieces of candy to those who received less than $8$ pieces of candy is $2:5.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434166 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434169 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1069 "q-235814" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1071 "![](images/38/38f113226c13332a07fdd6059819de5cf69147dbbfea3d1710325ef7776e5538.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1072 #uuid "348bf862-0000-5608-8f25-158f815d9723" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434182 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of pentagons to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of pentagons}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of pentagons. There are $4$ pentagons.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of pentagons to the total number of shapes is $4:7.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434183 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434170 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434183 1069 "q-101428" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434183 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434183 1071 "![](images/7b/7b309bd6e44f1a1bc2e179dbcf50e6672366f69be364ae55b482cea16c680553.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing numbers in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ hexagons for every $1$ pentagon." 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434183 1072 #uuid "86a8860d-3cfb-576b-a5c9-f9833c8b5308" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434183 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $4$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There is $1$ pentagon.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:1.$\n\nSo, the missing numbers are  $1$ and $4.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434184 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434162 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434184 1069 "q-132025" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434184 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434184 1071 "To make waffles, Joshua mixes $5$ eggs, $1$ cup of sugar, $200$ grams of butter, and $1$ cup of flour. What ratio describes the amount of sugar to the amount of flour?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434184 1072 #uuid "918c0ed9-8664-5aaa-af07-0b9b79fff05b" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434184 1074 "We can express the ratio of the amount of sugar to the amount of flour as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of sugar}:\\text{amount of flour}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of sugar. There is $1$ cup of sugar.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of flour. There is $1$ cup of flour.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of sugar to flour is $1:1.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434185 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434174 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434185 1069 "q-131916" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434185 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434185 1071 "![](images/b8/b8fb2d8be9596083481f83e6c8bacbb6a988ad527ef0a468583c239ea5e43838.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to the total number of shapes?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434185 1072 #uuid "94b6267e-404d-5206-b721-940a636b7569" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434185 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to total shapes is $2:7.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434186 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434173 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434186 1069 "q-60094" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434186 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434186 1071 "The table below represents the ages of players of a volleyball team. \n\n| Student | James | Robert | Charles | Daniel | Thomas | David |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Age (years) | $11$ | $9$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat is the ratio of players who are aged $10$ years or more to those who are less than $10$ years old?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434186 1072 #uuid "a57c2b2f-5eb9-5b18-919a-0a3e3924e394" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434186 1074 "From the table, there are $4$ players (James, Daniel, Thomas, David) whose age is $10$ or more years.\n\nThere are $2$ students (Robert, Charles)  whose age is less than $10$ years.\n\nSo the ratio of students whose age is $10$ or more years to those whose age is less than $10$ years is $4:2.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434187 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434164 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434187 1069 "q-59597" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434187 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434187 1071 "The ratio of chocolate chip cookies to total cookies in a bakeshop is $8:10.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434187 1072 #uuid "c0762ea5-0707-5974-8961-e278eb0de7ad" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434187 1074 "If the ratio of chocolate chip cookies to total cookies is $8:10,$ it means that there are $8$ chocolate chip cookies for every $10$ cookies in total.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $10$ cookies in the shop, $8$ of them are chocolate chip.\"" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434188 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434176 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434188 1069 "q-131946" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434188 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434188 1071 "To make a fruit sponge, Dimo mixes $3$ pounds of cherries with $2$ pounds of raisins. What ratio describes the amount of cherries to the amount of raisins?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434188 1072 #uuid "e2300841-eb93-50ec-a81c-b69a7df78772" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434188 1074 "We can express the ratio of the amount of cherry to the amount of raisins as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{amount of cherry}:\\text{amount of raisins}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the amount of cherries. There are $3$ pounds of cherries.\n\n- Next, we count the amount of raisins. There are $2$ pounds of raisins.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of cherries to raisins is $3:2.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434160 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434163 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1069 "q-235951" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1071 "A study group contains $5$ freshmen, $4$ sophomores, and $3$ juniors. What ratio describes the number of freshmen to the total number of students?\n\nThe required ratio is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1072 #uuid "e473c68b-cf42-5029-bb25-6a6af2c13e5a" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434189 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of freshmen to the total number of students as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of freshmen}:\\text{total number of students}\n$$\n\nWe compute our ratio as follows:\n\n- First, we count the number of freshmen. There are $5$ freshmen.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of students. There are $5+4+3=12$ students.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of freshmen to the total number of students is $5:12.$" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434190 1068 #edb/ref 17592186434167 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434190 1069 "q-101429" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434190 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434190 1071 "![](images/38/382d511b0797e5b5800bfabc45ab83be7c57439cfe8a4e76da7cfce7f6888661.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of circles to pentagons?" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434190 1072 #uuid "fa02dad0-56c6-5504-ac96-8894e78cb09f" 13194139534723 17592186045417 true] [17592186434190 1074 "We can express the ratio of the number of circles to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of circles}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of circles. There are $2$ circles.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There are $2$ pentagons.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of circles to pentagons 